  "comment": "Unified datetime (2026-10-09): the retired `date`/`date_range` types become ONE `datetime` type. A 'When' schema at default (day) precision and a 'Year' schema at year precision are created on a scratch workspace; the year/month/day chain for 2024-07-26 (and 2024-08-02 for the range end) is created first with deterministic ids (ensureDateChain pattern), then the value union is exercised end to end on one plain node: a full-day point {nodeId} (the default — no `time`), a timed point {nodeId, time: \"14:30\"}, an open range {start, end: null}, a range with a timed end slot, and a year-precision value on the YEAR node. Full-day is the absence of `time`; `time` is 24h wall-clock local at minute precision with no timezone, and requires day precision on both the schema ceiling and the slot's ref (fail-loud at the applier). The legacy date/date_range value shapes are legal members of the union, so no stored value needs rewriting. LOCKSTEP-PENDING: the strict enum change (`date`/`date_range` retired, `datetime` added) gates on the GTK/Flutter validators accepting `datetime` before the live migration runs.",
